            <ArticleTitle>Hemoperitoneum and acute abdomen caused by the rupture of ovarian granulosa cell tumor: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Granulosa cell tumors (GCT) constitute 70% of all ovarian sex-cord stromal tumors, which account for less than five percent of all ovarian carcinoma. The authors herein report a rare case of a ruptured GCT of the ovary in a 43-year-old female who was admitted to the emergency department with signs of acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
